-- title:
--   Rankin–Selberg unfolding on GL₂ with mixed majorant
-- statement:
--   Let $F$ be a number field and write $\alpha$ for the monoid homomorphism $(\mathbb{A}_F)^\times \to \mathbb{R}^\times$ obtained from the module (distributive Haar) character of the adele ring, assumed everywhere positive. Fix auxiliary data $D \subseteq \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_F)$, a family $U$ of subgroups indexed by ideals of $\mathcal{O}_F$ and a family $\mathrm{gen}$ indexed by the height-one spectrum; these enter only through the carrier record `productionPinsOf F D U gen (adelicBox F)`, whose measure-theoretic components are the Borel structure and Haar measure on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_F)$, the full central subgroup, and the adelic Haar measure conditioned on the box `adelicBox F`, so all Whittaker integrals below are taken against that conditional probability measure on $\mathbb{A}_F$. Let $\psi$ be an additive character of $\mathbb{A}_F$ that is trivial on $F$, continuous and non-trivial; let $\mu,\nu : (\mathbb{A}_F)^\times \to \mathbb{C}^\times$ have values of absolute value $1$ and be trivial on principal ideles; let $s \in \mathbb{C}$. Let $\varphi : \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_F) \to \mathbb{C}$ be continuous and an induced section for the pair $(\mu\,\alpha^{s+1/2},\ \nu\,\alpha^{-(s+1/2)})$, that is $\varphi(bg) = \mu(b_{11})\alpha(b_{11})^{s+1/2}\,\nu(b_{22})\alpha(b_{22})^{-(s+1/2)}\varphi(g)$ for all upper triangular $b$ and all $g$, and suppose that for every $g$ the Bruhat series $\sum_{\xi \in F} \|\varphi(w\,u(\xi)g)\|$ converges, where $w$ is the image of the Weyl element $\begin{pmatrix}0&1\\1&0\end{pmatrix}$ and $u(\xi)$ the upper unipotent matrix with entry $\xi$. Let $x,y : \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_F) \to \mathbb{C}$ be continuous and invariant under left translation by the image of $\mathrm{GL}_2(F)$, with the zeroth Whittaker coefficient of $x$ vanishing at every $g$ and with $a \mapsto \|W_a(x)(g)\|$ summable over $a \in F$ for every $g$. Let $w, d_1, d_2$ be real with $0 < d_1 < d_2$, and let $\mathcal{F}$ be contained in the determinant slab $\{g : \|\det g\| \in [d_1,d_2]\}$ and be a fundamental domain for the image of $\mathrm{GL}_2(F)$ with respect to Haar measure restricted to that slab. Assume two convergence hypotheses: the mixed folded majorant $\|x g\,\overline{y g}\|\bigl(\|\varphi(g)\| + \sum_{\xi}\|\varphi(w u(\xi) g)\|\bigr)\|\det g\|^{-w}$ is integrable on $\mathcal{F}$, and the unfolded integrand $\mathbf{1}_{\mathrm{slab}}(q.\mathrm{out})\,W_1(x)(q.\mathrm{out})\,\overline{W_1(y)(q.\mathrm{out})}\,\varphi(q.\mathrm{out})\,\|\det q.\mathrm{out}\|^{-w}$ is integrable over the orbit quotient of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_F)$ by the subgroup generated by the rational centre and the adelic unipotent subgroup, equipped with the quotient measure `rationalCentreUnipotentQuotientMeasure F`. The conclusion is the unfolding identity: the Petersson pairing over $\mathcal{F}$ at exponent $w$ of the product of $x$ with $\varphi(g) + \sum_{\xi \in F}\varphi(w u(\xi) g)$ against $y$, namely $\int_{\mathcal{F}} x(g)\bigl(\varphi(g)+\sum_\xi \varphi(w u(\xi) g)\bigr)\overline{y(g)}\,\|\det g\|^{-w}$, equals the integral over that quotient of the unfolded integrand just described.
--
--   This is the Rankin–Selberg unfolding step on $\mathrm{GL}_2$ over a number field: the pairing of a cusp form against the Bruhat-expanded Godement–Eisenstein series built from an induced section is rewritten as an integral of the product of the first Whittaker coefficients against the section over $Z(F)N(\mathbb{A})\backslash\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A})$, cut off by a determinant slab. It is the variant in which the convergence input is a single mixed majorant on the fundamental domain together with absolute integrability of the unfolded integrand, and it feeds the construction of the global $\mathrm{GL}_2 \times \mathrm{GL}_2$ Rankin–Selberg integral used in the Langlands–Tunnell part of the development.
